  "notes": "USAGE: Both senses are common. Context usually makes the meaning clear. When talking about rivers, it pairs with {下流|かりゅう} (downstream). When talking about social class, it pairs with {中流|ちゅうりゅう} (middle class) and {下流|かりゅう} (lower class).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {川|かわ}の{上流|じょうりゅう}: upper reaches of a river\n- {上流|じょうりゅう}{階級|かいきゅう}: upper class\n- {上流|じょうりゅう}{社会|しゃかい}: high society\n- {上流|じょうりゅう}{家庭|かてい}: upper-class family",
